      "title": "Swarm monitor",
      "notation": "swarm-monitor",
      "description": "Supervises any active swarm bound to a parent Swarm Work Item (`epic` or `milestone` in `beans`) on reactive completion wakeups and a 2-to-4-minute fallback timer: extracts live worker progress, checks CPU load, root disk headroom, and compressed or swapped memory footprint, halts runaway leaks or pulls the Andon cord on structural defects, assigns right-scoped non-heavy `idle-backlog` items to workers waiting on single-core compute without mid-build `git checkout`, refreshes and pushes the parent Swarm Work Item's Cold-Start Handover Runbook on every check-in (`swarm-epic-sync`), independently verifies completed branches before handing six-line merge requests to the merge steward, refills freed worker slots, and publishes standardized two-table human status reports (`on-demand` or `periodic`) free of session shorthands.",
